From 9172b5446015732f8c9b17161da90f4e0a8ceb89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Garfield <lucas@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:57:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sbom/spdx: fix sbom-grader findings for RPM-based images

sbom-grader (Red Hat ProdSec SBOM guide, generic_build/generic_release)
grades osbuild main's Fedora 44 qcow2 image SBOM D. Fix its findings:

- All packages have a supplier: emit supplier "Organization: <RPM Vendor>"
  (NOASSERTION when the RPM has no Vendor).
- RPM packages have packageFileName: record the RPM file name from the
  repo location in the dnf/dnf5 converters and emit packageFileName.
- Document passes extra validation: define every LicenseRef-* that an RPM
  License tag passes through (e.g. LicenseRef-Callaway-*) in
  hasExtractedLicensingInfos, and rewrite the invalid trailing '+' on a
  LicenseRef to '-or-later' (SPDX 2.3 Annex D).
- License list has correct form: emit creationInfo.licenseListVersion,
  the SPDX License List version bundled with license-expression.

With this the same SBOM grades A with no failed checks.
---
 osbuild/util/sbom/dnf.py         |  2 ++
 osbuild/util/sbom/dnf5.py        |  2 ++
 osbuild/util/sbom/spdx.py        | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 osbuild/util/sbom/spdx2/model.py | 26 +++++++++++++-----
 test/mod/test_util_sbom_spdx.py  |  7 +++--
 5 files changed, 72 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

